# rm512, the dry hood register (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm512
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_frida_bilgewell
written_by codex
title the dry hood register
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_oilcloth_up_in_clear_weather_and_logs_suspicions
likes crisp_apples dice sharp_knife autumn_wind
dislikes early_bells smoke
fears mistaking_an_impression_for_a_name
hopes a_record_whose_entries_can_stand_in_daylight
topics work +0.6 day +0.5 prices +0.3 weather +0.3
styles comfort=direct gossip=exact refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# tips the oilcloth brim clear of the eyes, keeps the voice even and distinguishes an observation from a name merely whispered.

words
oath! = Crease my oilcloth | File my apple core
saying! = A dry page can still carry a damp guess | Count the pips before announcing the throw
hood = the oiled hood | my stiff dark brim
page = a dry register leaf | a lined slip
pips = the little round pips | a clear pair of spots
die = a well-cut die | a bone cube
apple = a crisp green apple | a hard russet
peel = the smooth red peel | a translucent twist of fish skin
brim = the edge of the hood | the broad oilcloth brim
knife = a little paring knife | a clean-edged knife
haze = a dirty smoke haze | a belt of grey air
keyring = a plain key ring | a loop of cold iron
slate = my small slate | a dark square
ink = a plain black stroke | a fine ink line
line = a blank ruled space | a row left clear
chalk = a stub of chalk | a sharp little chalk end
cup = a clean drinking cup | a tin mug
cloth = a rag just for the ink | a plain wiping cloth
time = the measured hour | the shift's last mark
train = a row of wet prints | a trail across the flags

any
opinion @1 watch mixed 2 : A Watch mark on the page tells me who must answer for the entry. It doesn't turn a report into a witnessed fact.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : Even a House with fine coats may claim wealth and considerable influence. Neither ought to own the little blank where a witness writes a name.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A meal recorded as given should have been put within actual reach of the hungry wolf.
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : I can keep a clean conscience more easily by correcting the record than by polishing the cover.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : An unfamiliar name deserves the same accurate spelling as a familiar one.
opinion @1 city for 1 : A city big enough to keep records owes its residents records clear enough to question.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A fair sum and a clean coin can both stand being turned to the light.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : Festival noise pleases plenty of ears. Plain words still need somewhere to be heard.
opinion @1 times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : Hard days make the distinction between what a wolf owes and what a wolf can pay especially important.

grown
line @1 greet : There's a clear standing place level with my brim. | Welcome. Both eyes are visible under my brim today.
line @1 greet.return : Your greeting's recorded in the ordinary way, with another greeting.
line @1 again.open : Back before the ink from the first visit has dried.
line @1 farewell : Leave with your account made clear. | A sound step across the sheltered flags.
line @1 farewell.return : And a clear view ahead of your own hood.
line @1 react.news : Give me the account shorn of guesswork. | I'll hear what's actually reached you.
line @1 react.news.new : That wants its own fresh line.
line @1 react.news.known : I have the earlier appearance of that account in mind.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I wouldn't sign my own sight to that version.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : There are hard things to hear and harder things for somebody to live through.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That would earn a neat bright mark from me.
line @1 ask.how : How has your day looked under the brim?
line @1 answer.how : My eyes are clear and the hood is keeping its shape.
line @1 sympathise : I can take a plain statement at any pace you can manage.
line @1 reassure : Give your first line a margin for correction. Everybody ought to have that room.
line @1 refuse : I have an obligation ahead of that request in my book.
line @1 accept_decline : I won't make two entries out of a single refusal.
line @1 preclose : My next piece of business wants a hand free shortly.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while your remaining daylight is still in sight.
line @1 ack : That's an intelligible line right through the matter.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A stranger can stand here in clear view without owing an explanation.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : A greeting pitched below the unfortunate morning bell.
line @4 greet [here.time=night] : Enough lamplight under the brim for a civil word.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : I'd recognise the shape of your greeting through a yard of oilcloth.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here in plain sight of the turning!
line @1 thank : I'll set the good done against the trouble it cost you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had an obligation to attend and the means to meet it.
line @1 give.advice : Write the thing you saw before naming what you suspect.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I'm attending to one matter at a time with several waiting in clear view.
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Any part of your day that wants an attentive second look?
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the cell account clear of guesses. | I put a cup down where the receiver can see the rim.
b : What if a guess seems sound? | Why the rim?
a : Call it a guess. Ink isn't a reason to promote it. | So there's no question what has actually been offered.

scene exchange2
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wear the oilcloth in dry weather. | My hood's got a flattened spot above the left ear.
b : Can't you see clear sky? | Does it admit rain?
a : I observed the sky. I also observed it's capable of changing. | No. It shows where I've lifted the brim to look at something properly.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge an apple by the crack off the first bite. | I prefer an apple with its ordinary skin quite plain.
b : Wouldn't a gentle press suffice? | Why not polished?
a : It can tell me enough to buy it. Taste gets its own hearing. | The apple and the merchant may have different ideas of what shines.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a die resting on its edge another throw. | I like to clear the dice cup after each round.
b : Even a favourable edge? | Checking for a second die?
a : I want a whole number looking up when I count it. | Checking we've started over properly. A small habit's enough.

scene exchange5
when topic=work self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My knife is for an apple or a cut cord. | I inspect a clean edge before using it on supper.
b : Does it go with the register? | What do you seek?
a : No. I put it away when taking down an account. | A little nick that might turn a simple cut suddenly awkward.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn wind tests my hood stitching honestly. | I like the wind that clears a smoky street.
b : Any failed stitches? | Even if it takes your hat?
a : One tugged at the back. I repaired it before the next inspection by weather. | Oilcloth tied properly has listened to stronger proposals and stayed.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first stroke of an early bell stands recorded as unnecessary. | I can face an early shift more easily than an early bell.
b : Who authorised the finding? | They're close acquaintances.
a : My own ears. The official book has stayed closed. | One's a duty. The other insists on announcing it to every inch of my skull.

scene exchange8
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke obscures an honest view of an ordinary pair of hands. | I dry the oilcloth where it won't collect smoke.
b : Do you ask for a closer look? | Does oil keep the smell?
a : I move where the air's clear before I make any remark about what I saw. | It does a remarkable job of keeping things one hadn't requested.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a list that isn't in the public book. | I recall a mark with no proper witness beside it.
b : Does it name Houses? | Did you cross it out?
a : It names matters I haven't satisfied myself about. You'll hear no charge from a folded scrap. | I put the uncertainty beside it. Deleting a worry can also hide the truth.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.role=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a sharp difference between being held and being judged. | I ask the wolf giving a name to say it once slowly.
b : Does the book show it? | A new arrival?
a : It had better. A barred door doesn't supply a verdict. | New or familiar. The register shouldn't be guessing how anybody's called.

scene exchange11
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take the brim up far enough to look directly at a kindness. | An oath means more to me when the speaker knows the limits of sight.
b : Why notice kindness so carefully? | And admits them?
a : It ought to be remembered with the same accuracy as a fault. | Particularly then.

scene exchange12
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd count on a word from #self.friend# if my certainty runs too far. | A friend can share my quiet even under an unwelcoming hood.
b : Would that be welcome? | Do you lower it?
a : Better in private than after an incorrect public entry. | I raise it where my eyes can meet the other pair.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The claim is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. A claim is what arrived. | A rumour sometimes comes wrapped more carefully than the truth.
b : Do you have a finding? | Do you unfold it?
a : I have no warrant for turning those words into one. | I check who's prepared to stand beside the contents.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In lean times a small fine can seem dearer than a whole roof. | Hard days crowd the doorway with worries.
b : Does the amount change? | What comes first?
a : The listed sum stays plain. I can still listen to the circumstances. | The wolf needing to speak without a crowd deciding the answer first.

scene exchange15
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn the hood towards the wind on a long walk. | Give me elbow room for looking both ways on a walk.
b : Doesn't it spoil the hearing? | Expecting trouble?
a : I lift one corner when I need to listen. Weather and words get separate attention. | Walking is more pleasant when my shoulders don't have to steer my whole body.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a public book that has kept its corrections visible. | I hope every shaded corner in a public duty can bear some daylight.
b : A clean copy looks better. | Does that include your private list?
a : A clean-looking mistake hasn't improved for being neatly copied. | My list is for asking myself what I actually know, not accusing another wolf.

scene exchange17
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Northgate catches a crosswind that tests both sides of oilcloth. | I can draw the turn from the noises flags make in a shower.
b : Does the Sump get it too? | Which flags?
a : A curling turn of it. My lifted brim tells me on the walk home. | One lies over a hollow. It gives rain a different voice.

scene exchange18
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give my eyes an interval away from the small writing. | I stop a long count when the hand goes stiff.
b : Looking through a window? | Even on duty?
a : Or at a large plain apple. Whatever's far enough to make a change. | I mark the stopping place. A short pause is cheaper than entering the wrong total.

scene exchange19
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Each amount belongs to a stated purpose. | I turn the coin round before speaking to its worth.
b : Do you keep private prices too? | Don't know it by feel?
a : Only my supper's cost and the amount I owe the seller. | I can confirm what I feel without costing the payer anything.

scene exchange20
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I show a newcomer the waiting place with my whole paw. | A new name gets asked for in an even voice.
b : Why not point? | Even if you're rushed?
a : An open paw gives a clearer invitation than a sharp claw over my nose. | My haste has no authority to change a wolf's name.

scene exchange21
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The hood dries above a separate bit of floor. | My dice have a drawer well away from work papers.
b : To keep your rug clean? | Don't they fit?
a : To let the damp fall where I've already put the cloth. | They fit entirely too neatly. I'd like no question about what was used to reach a finding.

scene exchange22
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I choose dice with plain pips and no carved lettering. | I shake the cup once after the last roll.
b : For clarity? | Starting another game?
a : And so we discuss the score rather than the maker's sense of humour. | Proving nothing remains in the cup. Then my evening is my own.

scene exchange23
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I eat the apple at the counter's dry end. | A crooked cut means whoever shares gets the larger half.
b : Saving the book? | A fine for poor knife work?
a : And preserving the taste of the next page from my breakfast. | A simple way to make sure a mistake improves somebody's supper.

scene exchange24
when topic=work self.role=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set down the time I actually observed. | I look up before answering a question put through a door.
b : What about the time somebody else reports? | To see the speaker?
a : A separate entry naming its source. Two separate things can both matter. | To show the speaker at least one wolf is attending.

scene exchange25
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Winter makes a barred room feel colder even before frost. | In summer I give smoke a little less patience than usual.
b : What do you check? | Why summer?
a : Whether the blanket named on the page has actually reached the bench. | An open window can clear it. Somebody need only do the ordinary work of opening.

scene exchange26
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once had to correct a line I'd copied beautifully. | I keep a paper slip about an old doubtful account.
b : Did you hate spoiling the page? | To make a case one day?
a : I should have hated leaving an elegant error over somebody's name a great deal more. | To avoid forgetting I once had less evidence than I thought.

scene exchange27
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain rolls along my hood's hem before it drops. | I bring the slate under shelter before the rain changes shape.
b : Does that give any warning? | What changes first?
a : A little cold line alongside my ear. Enough to turn the page inwards. | The tiny misty drops become large enough to join two marks that ought to stay apart.

scene exchange28
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can speak quite frankly without giving another wolf's private history. | A corridor gets quieter when one wolf speaks plainly.
b : Where should that boundary run? | Does rank do that?
a : At what the visitor actually needs to know to understand the present business. | A plain account does rather more than a loud title.

scene exchange29
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I end the shift with my own record facing the lamp. | The hood goes on the peg facing out.
b : Looking for a skipped line? | Airing the lining?
a : Looking for any place my opinion has crept into a statement of fact. | Seeing that clear inner surface reminds me to put work away for a while.

scene exchange30
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome a day's pages ending with an honest full stop. | I can imagine the whole city asking plainly where money changed paws.
b : No loose ends? | Would you answer?
a : No hidden ones would be sufficient. | With the evidence I've truly got. My imagination isn't currency.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I wrote a name on a loose scrap in fine rain and watched the final letter run into the margin.
  : I could still recognise the name well enough to get it badly wrong.
  : I went back and asked again before copying a line into the proper book.
  b : Was your guess correct?
  : It was not. I kept the wet scrap by my ink for a week as an unusually effective reminder.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=dice]
  : A throw produced a four that appeared to have an extra pip. I put the cube beside the lamp and invited my partner to inspect the favourable little miracle.
  : One drop of rain had come off my hood and sat exactly where the fifth pip belonged.
  b : Was the score disputed?
  : I wiped the drop on my own sleeve, showed the four and passed the cup over. A very small public correction was sufficient.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples]
  : I cut an apple as squarely as I could to share between two hungry visitors. A little hard knot inside the fruit spoiled the apparent equality of the halves.
  : I sliced it across again and paired the thinner pieces off with the thick ones.
  b : Did anyone mind the extra cuts?
  : The plate went away quite clean. That was the extent of the evidence available and I found it satisfactory.

story tale4 [topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind]
  : A gust caught the loose hem of my oilcloth and knocked over a little closed tin. It rolled down three flags with a bang on every joint.
  : Wolves who had only heard the sound had three rather different notions of what had fallen.
  b : Which account went in your private book?
  : One tin, my hem, an autumn gust. The rest went away as a useful lesson about a noise heard round a corner.

story tale5 [topic=work self.job=guard]
  : A neat row of chalk marks looked to me like a count of meal cups. I turned the slate over and found the explanation carefully written on its reverse.
  : The marks meant freshly swept places on a bench. The cups had their own board.
  b : What changed after that?
  : I put every heading on the same face as its marks. Reading the back once was sensible. Requiring every reader to guess was not.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=guard
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cup delivered and recorded in that order. | An observation wants a date, a report wants a source.

rule @call2
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=guard
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear the margin before copying another name. | Blank where the evidence is blank.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the ink side of the page under oilcloth. | This hood has already earned its full day's keep.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The first bell is no witness to my readiness. | There is at least daylight enough for small pips.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.likes=crisp_apples
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A whole sound apple, one clean turn of the knife. | Good crisp fruit will answer for itself.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I want a little clear air before inspecting any fine marks. | See what the page says after the smoke lifts.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can hear an enquiry plainly across my open page.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember the name behind that familiar voice.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Keep inside the lamp light and we can both read plainly.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I ask no more about you than the business here requires.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=guard] : I keep the cells. My entries ought to show what actually happened to the wolf named on the line.
dlg @2 resident.job : I am responsible for noticing how accounts differ from events.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The public matter reported is #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The words passed along are #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I give no official finding on hearsay.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Go clear of smoke and with the particulars as you understood them.
dlg @1 watch.hub [here.wanted=yes] : The Watch has an entry against you for #here.fine# pennies. I'll state it plainly and let you ask about it.
dlg @2 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=yes] : I'm on watch. Give me the business you wish heard.
dlg @3 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=no] : This is my own time. I can hear a short enquiry without pretending the shift's begun.
dlg @1 watch.crime [here.witnessed=0] : Begin with what you personally saw. If there's a gap you may say there's a gap.
dlg @1 watch.reported [topic.reported=yes] : I've recorded the report as given. A report and a judgement remain separate matters.
dlg @1 watch.fine [here.wanted=yes] : The recorded fine is #here.fine# pennies. That is the sum shown against the entry.
dlg @2 watch.fine [here.wanted=no] : The fine register contains no amount due from you.
dlg @1 watch.bye : Carry away the actual account and leave the guesses here.
graft resident.hub
choice What good is a rain hood when the sky's clear? -> hood_register
node hood_register
say A clear sky has never given me a signed undertaking to remain in that condition. This way I can attend to my work without renegotiating with the weather.
free
choice Can you see properly under it? -> hood_register_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node hood_register_again
say The brim turns up. If I can't see properly I say so, which is a considerable improvement over filling in an account from imagination.
choice I'll leave the view clear. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft watch.hub
choice Why are hearing and seeing recorded separately? [self.job=guard] -> reported_seen
node reported_seen
say Because I may hear a perfectly true report without seeing any of the event. A reader needs to know where the words entered the record.
free
choice Do you leave a line empty? -> reported_seen_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node reported_seen_again
say If I lack an answer, yes. It is remarkably hard to mistake a deliberate blank for a signed statement after the reason has been written next to it.
choice Back to Watch matters. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
